#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:1
msgid "Cell-centered finite volume method on unstructured meshes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:3
msgid ""
"Supports triangles and quadrilaterals (2D), tetrahedra and hexahedra (3D).  "
"Operators:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:6
msgid ""
"**Laplacian** – Two-Point Flux Approximation (TPFA) with an implicit non-"
"orthogonal correction: the face normal is split as :math:`\\hat n = \\alpha "
"\\hat e + \\mathbf{k}` along the unit centroid-to-centroid direction :math:"
"`\\hat e`, so the normal derivative is :math:`\\alpha (u_j - u_i)/d + "
"\\mathbf{k}\\cdot\\nabla u_f` with the cross term taken from the Green-Gauss "
"gradient.  On orthogonal meshes :math:`\\mathbf{k} = 0` and this is plain "
"TPFA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:13
msgid "**Gradient** – Green-Gauss cell-centroid reconstruction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:14
msgid "**Divergence** – face-flux summation (adjoint of gradient)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:15
msgid ""
"**Boundary conditions** – ghost-cell (Dirichlet) / direct injection (Neumann)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:17
msgid ""
"Neumann boundary values on the named axis sides (``\"left\"``/``\"right\"``, "
"``\"front\"``/``\"back\"``, ``\"bottom\"``/``\"top\"``) are coordinate-"
"direction derivatives (:math:`\\partial u/\\partial x`, etc.), matching :"
"class:`pybamm.FiniteVolume`; e.g. ``u = x`` takes value ``+1`` on both "
"``\"left\"`` and ``\"right\"``.  Values on any other face tag (Gmsh region "
"names, ``\"iface_*\"``) are outward-normal derivatives :math:`\\partial u/"
"\\partial n`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured:25
msgid ""
"Passed through to :class:`pybamm.SpatialMethod`.  Additionally ``\"non-"
"orthogonal correction\"`` selects the decomposition of the face normal: "
"``\"over-relaxed\"`` (default, :math:`\\alpha = 1/\\cos \\theta`, favouring "
"diagonal dominance) or ``\"minimum\"`` (:math:`\\alpha = \\cos\\theta`, the "
"smallest cross term).  Both are exact on linear fields."
msgstr ""

