#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.div_D_grad:1
msgid "Discretise ``div(D * grad(u))`` as a single TPFA operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.div_D_grad:3
msgid ""
"Fully symbolic — works for both constant and state-dependent scalar ``D``. "
"Internal-face fluxes use the distance-weighted harmonic mean of ``D`` "
"(resistances in series, as :class:`pybamm.FiniteVolume` does for "
"coefficients of a gradient, so material interfaces carry the exact two-cell "
"flux) and the two-point normal derivative plus its non-orthogonal cross term "
"(see :meth:`_tpfa_matrix`).  ``D`` must be strictly positive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.div_D_grad:11
msgid ""
"This method is only reached when the expression is written as ``div(D * "
"grad(u))`` (a single product, matched syntactically during discretisation); "
"other flux forms go through the generic :meth:`gradient`/:meth:`divergence` "
"operators, which cannot apply boundary conditions conservatively and raise "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.divergence:1
msgid "Face-flux divergence of a cell-centred vector field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.divergence:3
msgid ""
"Boundary faces use zeroth-order flux extrapolation, so fluxes built from BC-"
"carrying gradients are rejected (see the raise below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.gradient:1
msgid ""
"Least-squares cell-centroid gradient, returned as a :class:`pybamm."
"VectorField` with one component per dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.gradient:4
msgid ""
"Exact on linear fields for any cell shape: every face contributes one "
"directional-derivative equation — towards the neighbour centroid (internal "
"faces), towards the face centroid holding the prescribed value (Dirichlet), "
"or the normal derivative itself (Neumann).  Boundary faces without a "
"condition contribute nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.gradient_squared:1
msgid "Pointwise ``|grad u|^2`` via :meth:`gradient`."
msgstr ""

