msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.internal_neumann_condition:1
msgid ""
"Normal gradient across the interface between two submeshes, one value per "
"interface face (outward from ``left_mesh``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.internal_neumann_condition:4
msgid ""
"On unstructured meshes this is the two-point difference plus the non-"
"orthogonal cross term (see :meth:`_tpfa_matrix`), whose face gradient is "
"fitted on both sides with the interface faces as cross-mesh rows.  "
"``left_bcs``/``right_bcs`` are the external boundary conditions of each "
"side, used by that fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.laplacian:1
msgid ""
"Laplacian ``Matrix @ discretised_symbol + bc_rhs``: the two-point flux plus "
"the non-orthogonal cross term, which is built from the BC-aware Green-Gauss "
"gradient so it stays fully implicit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.process_binary_operators:1
msgid ""
"Apply a binary operator componentwise when either operand is a :class:"
"`pybamm.VectorField`, lifting scalars to N components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.set_internal_bcs_for_concat:1
msgid ""
"Build internal BC dict for each ``Concatenation`` child by walking its "
"mesh's ``interface_data`` graph instead of assuming consecutive 1D-stack "
"pairs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.set_internal_bcs_for_concat:5
msgid ""
"Returns ``None`` when no ``iface_<other>`` face buckets exist in any child "
"mesh — that means there's no graph-discovered topology, so the caller should "
"fall through to the legacy 1D-stack pairwise routine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.set_internal_bcs_for_concat:10
msgid "For each child ``T_a`` on submesh ``mesh_a`` (graph case):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.set_internal_bcs_for_concat:11
msgid ""
"Pass through any user-supplied ``outer_bcs`` whose tag matches an external "
"boundary tag present in ``mesh_a.boundary_faces``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.set_internal_bcs_for_concat:13
msgid ""
"For each interface ``mesh_a ↔ mesh_b`` (one entry per neighbor in ``mesh_a."
"interface_data``), set ``iface_<b>`` to the discretised internal Neumann "
"gradient between ``T_a`` and the matching child ``T_b``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/spatial_methods/finite_volume_unstructured.py:docstring
#: of
#: pybamm.spatial_methods.finite_volume_unstructured.FiniteVolumeUnstructured.spatial_variable:1
msgid ""
"Return a vector of cell-centroid coordinates for ``symbol``'s direction (or "
"its leading name token, e.g. ``x_n`` -> ``x``), tiled over auxiliary "
"domains.  Raises :class:`pybamm.DomainError` rather than guessing when "
"neither identifies a coordinate."
msgstr ""
